## The safety boundary

The `no_trades_without_gate` validator enforces this rule at static-scan time:

> Any call to `order(`, `buy(`, `sell(`, `place_order(`, `submit_order(`, `cancel_order(`, or `place_trade(` MUST be preceded (in the same function body) by an explicit per-action gate — e.g. `if approved_in_session and user_typed_yes:`.

Generated code that puts a trade call behind only a config flag (no per-action user confirmation) **will fail validation**.

